Source: { "Type":"Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Modernize", "LastUpdated":"@EPOCH@", "Title":"webOS Chat Enabler (AIM)", "FullDescription":"Lets this device chat over webOS Chat, the community AIM service at oscar.webosarchive.org. Sign in to your webOS Account (with a public username, not just an email) and a webOS Chat account appears in Accounts and signs in to Messaging by itself: no screen name or password to type. It follows your webOS Account: signing out removes the chat account, and a new pass phrase from your account page is picked up within the hour.<br><br>For webOS CE 3.1.0 and later. Adds libpurple's AIM plugin, the webOS Chat account type and a small background service. Nothing appears in the Launcher. A restart is needed after install, update and removal.", "MinWebOSVersion":"3.1.0", "PostInstallFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostUpdateFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostRemoveFlags":"RestartDevice" }
